  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "The basic color of the small leaves is a rich green with white variegation. The white ranges from completely covering the leaf to patches, streaks, or flecks. In the spring, the variegations emerge pink, turning to white, cream, and yellow. The name means \"five-colored maple. \""
